{"id":"319611234","kind":"article","title":"谬误：你需要每天使用 SuperMemo 学习","author":"Piotr Wozniak","original_authors":["Piotr Wozniak"],"original_source_urls":["https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Myth:_You_need_to_learn_with_SuperMemo_every_day"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"间隔重复 & 注意力管理","date":"2020-11-29","updated":"2026-10-27","votes":45,"comment_count":15,"minutes":1,"chars":269,"keywords":["SuperMemo","间隔重复","渐进阅读","可提取性"],"summary":"条目反驳“必须每天使用 SuperMemo”的说法：停用一段时间会影响新材料，长期知识的可提取性下降较慢；作者称，延迟与优先队列等机制出现前的每日使用建议更多出于心理考虑，同时提醒部分间隔重复实现会惩罚漏复习，并建议了解渐进阅读。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/319611234","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"谬误"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"事实"},{"id":"sec-3","level":2,"title":"起源"},{"id":"sec-4","level":2,"title":"改进措施"}],"html":"<h2 id=\"sec-1\">谬误</h2><p data-pid=\"4GY5nXak\">你需要每天使用 SuperMemo</p><h2 id=\"sec-2\">事实</h2><p data-pid=\"NZt9WNlm\">如果你停止使用 SuperMemo 一段时间，你的平均知识保留率就会下降。对于长期使用的人来说，休息几天几乎不会引起注意。它只会影响新材料。旧材料的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Retrievability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">可提取性</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>下降得非常慢。</p><h2 id=\"sec-3\">起源</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"_CcVDTE_\">在引入<b>延迟</b><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>或<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Priority_queue\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">优先队列</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>等概念之前，建议用户每天使用 SuperMemo。这更多的是出于心理上的原因，而不是实际的原因。大多数中途放弃的人都是从短暂的休息开始的，而且休息的时间会越来越长。<br/><br/></li><li data-pid=\"vl50ffoa\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Spaced_repetition\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>的一些实现会惩罚错过重复的用户。</li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-4\">改进措施</h2><p data-pid=\"Lk9ECSih\">阅读有关<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Incremental_reading\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">渐进阅读</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>的内容。</p><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 记忆可提取性 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"559819340\" href=\"#/post/559819340\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 延迟 <a href=\"https://www.yuque.com/supermemo/wiki/postpone\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.yuque.com/supermemo/wiki/postpone</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 优先级队列 <a href=\"https://www.yuque.com/supermemo/wiki/priority_queue\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.yuque.com/supermemo/wiki/priority_queue</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 间隔重复 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"305651556\" href=\"#/post/305651556\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 增量阅读 <a href=\"https://www.yuque.com/supermemo/wiki/incremental_reading\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.yuque.com/supermemo/wiki/incremental_reading</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"315758950","title":"谬误：SuperMemo 的重复会浪费太多时间","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":32,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"352083787","title":"谬误：在第一天就多次复习你的材料","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":11,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"559819340","title":"记忆可提取性","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":8,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"305651556","title":"间隔重复 (spaced repetition)","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":38,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"279166945","title":"间隔效应","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":21,"minutes":3,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「间隔重复」· Andy Matuschak"},{"id":"322673517","title":"示范：我的渐进阅读工作流程","author":"Master How To Learn","votes":207,"minutes":11,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「渐进阅读」· Master How To Learn"},{"id":"562780743","title":"通过间隔重复生成问题","author":"Issa Rice","votes":8,"minutes":1,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「渐进阅读」· Issa Rice"}],"rec_answers":[]}